DOLLY 7
PACKAGE voice
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
REQUIRES HOST microphone@0
REQUIRES HOST pty@0
REQUIRES HOST touch@0
REQUIRES HOST threads@0

# voice as speech-build links it against transcribe.cpp, with the model it
# reads: buttons and speech in the place of a keyboard, for a terminal program.
FROM /v0.1.4/demos/speech/Dollyfile-speech-build 2a3870470d7be213d8fedc10f87d2fbb6bbf2cbaef3b12734425a7d2fd23cfee
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/speech/Dollyfile-parakeet 45ac10e361a0746ba603aef41eedb00a06bd70c2a1cc76894e4dbda68995e7f5

EXPORTS TOOL   voice
EXPORTS FOLDER transcribe-licenses /usr/share/licenses/transcribe.cpp
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/voice.1
    voice: runs a terminal program in all but the terminal's last rows, where it
    draws buttons that a finger taps, and types what each says, or what is
    said, into the program: transcribe.cpp with NVIDIA's Parakeet model.
    
      voice MENU [MODEL.gguf] -- PROGRAM [ARG...]
    
    In MENU, "[NAME] caption" begins a page of buttons and "LABEL = TEXT" is a
    button that types TEXT (\r Enter, \e Escape, \t Tab, \xHH a byte, \w a wait
    of 0.4 s). After the text, :speak listens and types what was said, :word
    types it as a search word and :page NAME shows another page. pi-phone's
    /etc/dolly/pi.menu is one. PROGRAM runs on a pseudo-terminal; the keyboard
    and a paste still reach it. It needs touch@0, pty@0 and microphone@0; the
    microphone is open only while it listens, and nothing that is said leaves
    the page.
